    "q-67819": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67819",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is natural number\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is an integer\n\nIII. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is a rational number",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not an integer.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is a rational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
