      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $\\frac{3}{2}$\n\nII. $-3$\n\nIII. $5$",
      "worked_solution": "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $-3$ and $5$ are integers, but $\\frac{3}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
